<title>ITALY: ATHLETICS-KENYA'S TERGAT WINS WORLD CROSS COUNTRY TITLE.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-KENYA'S TERGAT WINS WORLD CROSS COUNTRY TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenya's Paul Tergat won the senior men's race at the world cross country championships on Sunday in an unofficial time of 35 minutes 11 seconds.</p>
<p>Morocco's Salah Hissou was second and Kenya's Thomas Nyariki third.</p>
</text>
